.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-payouts-resend - Re-broadcast the signed transfer a submit stored


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 payouts resend  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Re-broadcast the signed transfer the gateway stored on submit, after the node
refused it or did not answer. The same bytes, so the same nonce and hash: it can be
mined once at most, and resending is always safe. Nothing is signed again.

.PP
422 payout_not_signed when nothing is stored: sign it with 'payouts submit \&'.

.PP
-w/--wait follows the payout until confirmed or failed, as in 'payouts send'.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for resend

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=15m0s
	Max time to wait when --wait is set; unset, 10× the chain's measured p90 settlement, kept within 5m–15m

.PP
\fB-w\fP, \fB--wait\fP[=false]
	Block until the operation confirms on-chain (or fails)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 payouts resend <payout_id>
  rail0 payouts resend <payout_id> --wait
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-payouts(1)\fP
